  "question": {
    "text": "An expression of energy density is given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>&#946;</mi></mfrac><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></math>&nbsp;are constants, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is displacement, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math> is Boltzmann constant and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math> is the temperature. The dimensions of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi></math> will be",
